CM 40 m two-element phased vertical array over perfect ground
CM Quarter-wave verticals a quarter wavelength apart along X, fed 90 degrees
CM apart for a cardioid pattern toward +X (toward the lagging element)
CM The EX voltages force equal currents in quadrature at 7.15 MHz despite
CM mutual coupling; they were computed for these dimensions, so recompute
CM them after changing vert_len or spacing. Note the unequal feed impedances.
CE
SY vert_len=10.2, spacing=10.48
SY rad=0.0125
GW 1 21 0 0 0 0 0 vert_len rad
GW 2 21 spacing 0 0 spacing 0 vert_len rad
GE 1
GN 1
EX 0 1 1 0 1.0 0.0
EX 0 2 1 0 2.1154 -1.3339
FR 0 31 0 0 7.0 0.01
RP 0 19 73 1000 0 0 5 5
EN
